  "result": "Perfect! All 127 tests pass \u2705\n\n**Payment terms are fully integrated:**\n\n**Added lastDayOfMonth() to src/dates.js** \u2014 Calculates the last day of a month (UTC)\n```javascript\nlastDayOfMonth('2026-10-15')  // \u2192 '2026-10-31'\nlastDayOfMonth('2024-02-15')  // \u2192 '2024-02-29' (leap year)\nlastDayOfMonth('2025-02-15')  // \u2192 '2025-02-28' (non-leap year)\n```\n\n**Updated createInvoice()** \u2014 Accepts optional terms and calculates due dates\n- Default: `terms = 'NET30'`\n- Valid terms: `'NET14'`, `'NET30'`, `'EOM'`\n- Calculates and stores `invoice.dueDate`:\n  - **NET14**: issue date + 14 days\n  - **NET30**: issue date + 30 days\n  - **EOM**: last day of issue month\n- Returns TERMS_INVALID for unknown terms\n\n**Example:**\n```javascript\nconst invoice = createInvoice({\n  customerId: 'C-001',\n  issueDate: '2026-10-07',\n  lines: [...],\n  terms: 'NET14'\n})\n// invoice.dueDate = '2026-10-21'\n\nconst invoice2 = createInvoice({\n  customerId: 'C-001',\n  issueDate: '2026-10-15',\n  lines: [...],\n  terms: 'EOM'\n})\n// invoice2.dueDate = '2026-10-31'\n```\n\n**Error code added:**\n- `TERMS_INVALID` \u2014 terms must be NET14, NET30, or EOM\n\n**Test coverage (10 new tests):**\n- lastDayOfMonth for various months\n- Leap year and non-leap year handling\n- NET14 due date calculation\n- NET30 due date calculation\n- EOM due date calculation\n- Month boundary handling\n- Invalid terms rejection",
